# geocode-glib -- forward and reverse geocoding, and the first of the three
# packages the Weather and Location settings sit on.
#
# It is here for libgweather, which needs it to turn a place name into
# coordinates; libgweather in turn is what gnome-control-center's Weather
# integration and gnome-shell's weather section read.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/geocode-glib/3.26/geocode-glib-3.26.4.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=2d9a6826d158470449a173871221596da0f83ebdcff98b90c7049089056a37aa
SRC_DIR=geocode-glib-3.26.4

# EVERY OPTION IN THIS PROJECT IS A PLAIN BOOLEAN DEFAULTING TRUE. There is not
# a single meson `feature`/auto in meson_options.txt, so the hazard here is not
# ambient detection (finding 4) but finding 3: DOING NOTHING TURNS EVERYTHING
# ON.
#
# -Dsoup2=false IS THE ONE THAT WOULD ACTUALLY BREAK. The option defaults
# **true**, and this tree has libsoup 3.6.5 and no libsoup2 at all -- so the
# default asks for a library nobody packaged. It is also the reason to read this
# file rather than assume: libgweather, packaged in this same wave from the same
# upstream for the same consumer, defaults soup2 to FALSE. Two projects, same
# ecosystem, opposite defaults for the same option name.
#
# -Denable-gtk-doc=false: gtk-doc is not packaged.
#
# -Denable-installed-tests=false: installs test programs under
# /usr/share/installed-tests. Two packages owning the same path is a hard
# install error with no override, and half of GNOME ships into that directory --
# the directory itself is safe (tape skips directory entries when building the
# conflict list) but identically-named FILES under it are not. Nothing here
# wants them.
#
# -Denable-introspection=true is stated rather than inherited: it equals the
# default, gobject-introspection is packaged, and the .gir/.typelib are what a
# GJS consumer would resolve. Naming it means an image without introspection
# fails here rather than producing a quietly smaller package.
MESON_ARGS="-Dsoup2=false \
-Denable-introspection=true \
-Denable-gtk-doc=false \
-Denable-installed-tests=false"
